## What I checked

I read the brief and applied Daniel's bar. I opened every file in `pages/`. I opened both files of
each extra row and the Nan look reference. I opened the nine reference sheets in `refs/`.

I counted every pixel that is not 0 and not 255 in all twenty-one line files. I measured the
stroke depth in every line print with a distance transform. I measured the width of every
enclosed white region. I measured the object box and the frame edges of every color print.

## Line file count

The count is 0 in all twenty-one line files. No gray, no specks, no shading.

## Thick ring and band

A stroke wider than 40 px would show in my depth scan. No such stroke exists in any line print.
The solid black areas are the eye pupils, and one dog nose. The bar allows both.

## Line gap

No line print holds a white region too thin to color. The bus and K1 hold one hairline speck
each. Both are a few pixels wide. Neither is a coloring problem.

## The bus shadow

The bus color print carries a hard gray cast shadow. It covers 4.72 percent of the frame.
The line art has no shadow and no ground line. The shadow reads as a shadow at book size.
The bar lists gray only in the line art, so I made this a note and lowered the rating.

## The sun

The eight rays are sharp triangles. The wide base of each triangle sits on the disc line.
The point faces outward. At book size the line art reads as a sun and not as a flower.
This fixes the week 2 flower failure.

## The cat eyes

The left eye is narrower than the right eye in the line art. The color file shows the same
difference. The head turns to the left, so the far eye sits at an angle. The brief says
that foreshortening is correct. A note, not a defect.

## The fish

The tail fin has a wavy outline in the line art. The color file draws the same scalloped fin.
A small smile mark sits at the mouth. The color file shows no mouth line. The mark is small
and the fish still reads as a fish. Notes, not defects.

## The pen and the pencil

The pen shows a clip and a rounded cap end. The pencil shows an eraser, a band, a wood cone
and a lead point. The two do not look alike at book size. The spec asks for a rounded cap end.

## K1 the practice line

The head faces the right edge, the other way from the nose check row. The nose shows in the
color file as a bump with a nostril line. The nose also shows in the line file as a bump in
the profile contour. The ear is an open C arc and the eyebrow is a thick stroke. The bar
lists both as marks that are not a defect.

## K2 the nose page, defect

The color file shows the nose. The line file draws no nose contour. The fingertip stands
where the nose should be. The text names the nose, so the face part must show in both files.
This row fails.

The fixed line file already exists. It sits at
`out/storytime/l2/unit1/w01/delivery-muse-v2/l2-w01-story-page-a-nose-line-v2.png`.
It adds a closed round nose bump at the finger tip. The approved record names that file
as the line print for this row.

## K3 the nut page

One big brown acorn rests on the open palm. The nut, the hand and Nan read in both files.
Nan keeps her reference look in both files. No hand shows six digits.

## Retry hint for K2

Draw a closed round nose bump at the finger tip in the line art, as the color file shows,
and keep the finger touching it.

